  "slug": "tuning-neuronal-61d2",
  "summary": "Three preprints map defined feedback and signaling rules onto epithelial, prostate cancer and cell-assembly collective outcomes.",
  "synthesis": "Across three preprints, collective outcomes are traced to defined local rules rather than global parameters. In epithelial monolayers, an active vertex model combined with experiments attributes glassy dynamics to crowding coupled with a mechanochemical feedback loop (MCFL-1). In prostate cancer, a mathematical model couples EMT regulators, androgen receptor and Notch-Jagged/Delta signaling, showing that AR stabilizes a hybrid epithelial/mesenchymal phenotype in the presence of Notch-Jagged signaling. A simulation framework links adhesion, motility and stiffness to cell self-assembly and predicts optimal motility for clusters. The systems differ in scale and method, so the shared thread is conceptual: mapping explicit feedback and signaling rules onto population-level behavior. What is new is the rule-level mapping from mechanistic components to collective states.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-15"
}
